        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(telegram): fall back for web apps outside DMs",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Telegram group, channel, or unconfirmed targets could receive a native Web App inline button that Telegram only accepts in private chats, causing delivery to be rejected.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTelegram now emits native Web App buttons only after the delivery target is confirmed as a direct chat. Group and unknown targets keep the original message and receive the portable HTTPS link as text; the low-level encoder also fails closed when chat context is absent.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDirect-message Web Apps continue to open natively. Group, channel, and unresolved targets receive an understandable link fallback instead of a Telegram API error.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- 71 focused Telegram presentation/outbound tests passed on exact head after the final rebase: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29669041067\n- Full changed gate passed, including extension production/test typechecks, extension lint, formatting, plugin boundaries, and import-cycle checks: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29668866624\n- Fresh autoreview passed with no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I understand and reviewed the complete change.\n",
